1. I’d go with liquid cooling for the GPU in this build.  
2. It does a better job of handling heat during those long gaming and streaming sessions, like watching IPL matches while playing at the same time.  
3. The temps stay more stable under heavy graphics loads, so the card doesn’t get as hot or throttle as easily.  
4. it costs more and needs a bit of extra care, but for a high-performance gaming PC still a solid choice if I want the best cooling.
